; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Lissajous Figures
; CATEGORY: Spirals & Curves
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     lissajous, sine, parametric curves, animation, oscilloscope
; SUMMARY:  Draws a table of Lissajous figures, the curves made by two sine waves at right angles, and slowly turns them like an oscilloscope.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Move a point left and right with one sine wave and up and down
;   with another. If the two waves have different speeds you get a
;   Lissajous figure. The table shows every pair of speeds from 1 to
;   4 across and 1 to 3 down. The second wave keeps sliding a little
;   ahead of the first (its "phase" changes), so all the figures
;   seem to spin in 3D, the way they did on old oscilloscope screens.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run and watch. Press Stop to end. Look at the row and
;   column: the figure crosses itself in a way that tells you both
;   speeds.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * parametric curves: x and y both worked out from a third number t
;   * x = sin(a x t + phase), y = sin(b x t)
;   * equal speeds give an ellipse; speeds 1 and 2 give a figure eight
;   * animation by redrawing everything with a slightly changed phase
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Stop the phase at 90 and look at each figure carefully.
;   * Add a column for speed 5.
;   * Draw only the 3 by 2 figure, very big, with a thick pen.
; ============================================================

make "cellsize 150
make "half 58

; One figure centered at (cx, cy).
to figure :a :b :phase :cx :cy
  penup
  for [t 0 360 4] [
    setxy :cx + :half * sin :a * :t + :phase :cy + :half * sin :b * :t
    pendown
  ]
end

; Labels for the speeds along the top and down the side.
to labels
  setpencolor [90 160 90]
  for [a 1 4] [penup setxy -230 + :cellsize * (:a - 1) 225 label :a]
  for [b 1 3] [penup setxy -340 145 - :cellsize * (:b - 1) label :b]
end

to frame :phase
  clean
  labels
  setpencolor [120 255 140]
  for [b 1 3] [for [a 1 4] [
    figure :a :b :phase -225 + :cellsize * (:a - 1) 150 - :cellsize * (:b - 1)
  ]]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [10 25 15]
setpensize 2
setlabelheight 16
make "phase 0
forever [
  frame :phase
  make "phase remainder :phase + 2 360
  wait 2
]
